# The task stack is an append-at-the-top list of `## T-<date>-<slug>` entries,
# so every parallel lane writes at the same place and every lane after the
# first conflicts there. A line-level merge interleaves two entries into
# nonsense; this driver merges whole entries and, because git hands it the
# ancestor, tells "new on one side" apart from "the other side deliberately
# moved it to done.md" — the case a blind union resurrects.
#
# The driver command is per-clone git config, which a repository cannot ship.
# `pnpm prepare` runs scripts/setup-merge-driver.sh, which sets it.
specs/tasks/active.md merge=taskstack
specs/tasks/done.md   merge=taskstack
